WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:12.403
Grace gazed at the big painting of a dancer.

2
00:00:12.423 --> 00:00:15.184
"That's beautiful!"

3
00:00:15.304 --> 00:00:16.424
she said.

4
00:00:16.444 --> 00:00:32.925
"When I get older, I want to be an artist."

5
00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.870
Grace and Dad were at an art museum in Boston.

6
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:43.273
Grace suddenly noticed an empty frame on a wall.

7
00:00:44.554 --> 00:00:46.756
Then she noticed another empty frame.

8
00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:51.079
"Dad?" Grace asked.

9
00:00:51.099 --> 00:00:54.121
"Why are those frames empty?"

10
00:00:54.141 --> 00:00:58.004
"Their paintings are missing," said Dad.

11
00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.181
"Actually someone stole them."

12
00:01:03.322 --> 00:01:04.063
She gasped.

13
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:09.426
"Really?" A museum guard walked over.

14
00:01:09.446 --> 00:01:15.109
"It was the biggest art theft in American history," he said.

15
00:01:15.129 --> 00:01:17.730
"When did it happen?"

16
00:01:18.271 --> 00:01:19.211
Grace asked.

17
00:01:21.813 --> 00:01:24.714
"March 18, 1990," said the guard.

18
00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.216
"Two thieves came late at night.

19
00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:29.977
They were dressed as police officers.

20
00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:34.658
So a museum guard let the men inside.

21
00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:44.581
The thieves stole paintings, sketches, a bronze eagle, and a small vase.

22
00:01:50.982 --> 00:01:54.223
All together the items are worth about fifty million dollars."

23
00:01:56.164 --> 00:01:58.244
"Whoa," said Grace.

24
00:01:58.264 --> 00:02:00.925
"That's a lot of money.

25
00:02:01.585 --> 00:02:03.726
I guess the thieves knew what to steal!"

26
00:02:03.746 --> 00:02:10.128
"The men did steal some valuable artwork," said the guard.

27
00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:14.169
"But they left more valuable artwork behind.

28
00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.031
Many people think the thieves didn't know much about art."

29
00:02:21.851 --> 00:02:23.031
"Were the men ever caught?"

30
00:02:23.512 --> 00:02:24.652
asked Grace's dad.

31
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.541
The guard shook his head.

32
00:02:27.561 --> 00:02:30.122
"The police had several suspects.

33
00:02:30.542 --> 00:02:31.743
But they never caught anyone.

34
00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:36.806
Workers at the museum decided to hang four empty frames.

35
00:02:39.748 --> 00:02:42.009
The frames remind everyone of the stolen paintings.

36
00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.511
We hope to get them back someday."

37
00:02:48.233 --> 00:02:49.593
Grace looked at Dad.

38
00:02:49.613 --> 00:02:53.275
"I don't want to be an artist anymore.

39
00:02:55.602 --> 00:02:57.348
I want to be a detective.

40
00:02:57.749 --> 00:03:00.198
And I want to solve this case!"
